@jieai/dsh-plugin-vet README · Deployment postures: what is kept, what is *not* promised (0.5.12)：The table above is the `profile` preset. Below is the **posture** — a different question: "how protected am I
right now?" Any claim of "protected / blocked / covered" has to land on one of these rows; if it cannot, it is
not said.

@jieai/dsh-plugin-vet README · Deployment postures: what is kept, what is *not* promised (0.5.12)：In one line: **scan-only sees "what this code says", standard blocks family 1/2's irreversible destruction
(deleting your keys, a confirmed mass-destruction loop), hardened starts watching "what it is doing", and only
adding `mode: deny` is allowed to say "it does not get installed" — none of the four means "it cannot hurt me".**

@jieai/dsh-plugin-vet README · Deployment postures: what is kept, what is *not* promised (0.5.12)：Which of the four stops which disaster is tabulated once, above, in
[What a bad plugin actually does to you](#which-of-the-three-vet-actually-stops--and-in-which-mode). This
paragraph does not restate it — that is how the two versions drifted apart last time.

@jieai/dsh-plugin-vet README · Capability boundary (honest list)：> Static scanning is a "speed bump + forensics layer", not a security boundary. The following is split by
> **impact on the verdict**, and the forms it **explicitly does not detect** are listed truthfully (all
> empirically verified).

@jieai/dsh-plugin-vet README · Platform Support：The one-glance matrix — what actually runs where. T1 = out-of-process sentinel (samples memory /
child-process count / fd every tick and alarms); T2 = in-process hooks (interception, honeypot, GUI
shield); panel = live host-metrics display (`metrics.js`).
